# C# Conventions

## Namespaces
- Use file-scoped namespaces (`namespace Foo;` not `namespace Foo { }`)

## Logging
- Use `ILogger<T>` for all logging -- never `Console.WriteLine`
- Use structured logging: `_logger.LogDebug("Value {Name}", value)` not string interpolation

## Records and Immutability
- Prefer `init` over `set` for record properties
- Do not add mutable `{ get; set; }` to record types unless absolutely necessary

## Error Handling
- Never use `async void` except for event handlers, and always wrap body in try/catch
- In Blazor components, use `await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged)` for thread safety

## Naming
- Spelling matters: "Saturation" not "Satuation", "Block" not "Bock"
- Use PascalCase for public members, _camelCase for private fields
- Constants: PascalCase (e.g. `MaxRetryCount`) not UPPER_SNAKE

## DI Lifetimes
- Use `AddScoped` for interpreter services in Blazor WASM (behaves as singleton)
- `AddTransient` only for truly stateless services

## Null Safety
- Nullable is enabled project-wide -- respect it
- Always null-check optional fields before access (e.g. `_field?.Property`)
